window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>A day at a Tampa festival brings laughter and questions for Hali Waverly and Gray Hunter. Fun and games lead to a fortune teller, who warns them of incoming trouble.</p> <p>Hali laughs it off, but when they get home, they find the police have shut down the road in front of Paradise Lodge. There’s a body in the median, and Hali knows the victim. In fact, the dead witch is a member of her grandmother’s coven. But why was the victim so close to Hali’s home? Was she trying to warn her of something?</p> <p>Hali and Gray start digging and find things they weren’t expecting, including an undercover group of witches and warlocks selling their services at area farmer’s markets.</p> <p>The mystery only deepens when the victim’s body goes missing…and shows up again on the beach, this time with two other dead witches. This isn’t zombies, though, it’s ghouls…and somebody is raising them for a very specific purpose.</p> <p>The deeper Hali digs, the closer to home she gets. She assumes her newest enemy Hester is behind the ghouls, but the truth is much more nefarious.</p> <p>St. Pete Beach is about to be overrun with the dead. Sadly, the enemy might be the last person Hali ever expected.</p>"; 
